course: dictionary
lesson: 1804
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. Cloud is a good example. In «Thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing», cloud means a white or grey mass in the sky made of tiny water drops. The words sky, storm and freezing are the clues.
explain: Now look at a different clue. «A cloud over the day» has no real cloud in it. It means something that makes people sad or worried. The word over and the feeling of the phrase tell you it is about mood, not weather.
explain: Context also shows you whether cloud is a noun or a verb. «The white cloud above a kettle is tiny droplets» uses cloud as a noun, a thing you can name. «By evening the sky began to cloud over» uses cloud as a verb, an action meaning to become cloudy. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Cloud can be a noun (a cloud, clouds) or a verb (to cloud, cloud over).
fact: A cloud in the sky is made of millions of tiny water drops or ice crystals.
fact: In the water cycle, water evaporates, cools and turns into clouds, then falls as rain, snow or hail.
fact: «Cloud» can also mean something that makes people sad or worried, as in «a cloud over the day».
fact: In computing, «the cloud» means computers on the internet where you store your files.
exercise: «Thunderstorm clouds reach so high that their tops are far below freezing.» What does cloud mean here? | Computers on the internet where you store files | *A white or grey mass in the sky made of tiny water drops | Something that makes people sad | A mass of smoke from a bonfire that hides the sun
exercise: Mum says, «There has been a cloud over the day since the phone call.» What does cloud mean? | *Something that makes people sad or worried | Steam from a kettle | A white mass in the sky | Computers on the internet
exercise: «By evening the sky began to cloud over.» What does cloud mean? | *To become cloudy | A white mass of tiny drops | Computers that store files | Something that makes people sad
test: Ella saves her homework to the cloud. What does cloud mean? | To become cloudy | A grey mass in the sky | *Computers on the internet where you store files | A mass of dust in the air
test: «Steam is invisible: the white cloud above a kettle is tiny droplets.» What is the white cloud made of? | Invisible steam | Smoke from the kettle | Dust from the kitchen | *Tiny droplets of water
exam: Jayden says cloud always means the sky. What is the best answer? | No, cloud only means a storm | Yes, but only in poems | *No, cloud can also be a verb, a worry, or the internet | Yes, cloud always means the sky and nothing else
